  "voiceover": {
    "local_output_path": "outputs/video-assets/gradient-descent-warm-minimal-lesson-edit-v1.voiceover.wav",
    "text": "Gradient descent is how AI learns from mistakes. First, the model makes a wrong prediction. That mistake becomes a loss score. The loss curve shows how different weight settings create different errors. The gradient points toward higher loss, so the update moves the opposite way. One small step changes the weight a little. The loss becomes lower, but not perfect. Training repeats many small steps. If the step is too large, it can overshoot. That is gradient descent: repeated careful steps toward lower error."
  },
